# Carbon Design System Agent Rules

## What this project is
This is a Storybook component library built on IBM Carbon Design System (@carbon/react).
The running Storybook is at http://localhost:6006.
All UI must use Carbon components and tokens only — never arbitrary colours, custom components, or external UI libraries.

## Available components (import from @carbon/react)
Button, TextInput, PasswordInput, Form, FormGroup, Stack,
DataTable, Table, TableHead, TableRow, TableHeader, TableBody, TableCell, TableContainer,
TableToolbar, TableToolbarContent, TableToolbarSearch, DataTableSkeleton,
Modal, InlineNotification, ToastNotification, ActionableNotification,
Tag, Checkbox, Tile, Accordion, AccordionItem,
Dropdown, MultiSelect, ComboBox,
Select, SelectItem, DatePicker, DatePickerInput,
Toggle, RadioButton, RadioButtonGroup,
Breadcrumb, BreadcrumbItem, Link,
Grid, Column,
Loading, InlineLoading, SkeletonText, SkeletonPlaceholder,
Tabs, TabList, Tab, TabPanels, TabPanel,
Header, HeaderContainer, HeaderName, HeaderNavigation, HeaderMenuItem,
HeaderGlobalBar, HeaderGlobalAction, HeaderMenuButton, HeaderSideNavItems, SkipToContent,
SideNav, SideNavItems, SideNavLink, SideNavMenu, SideNavMenuItem

## Available icons (import from @carbon/icons-react)
Add, TrashCan, Download, Edit, Search, Settings, User, ChevronDown,
ChevronRight, Close, Warning, CheckmarkFilled, ErrorFilled, InformationFilled

## Carbon token reference (NEVER use arbitrary hex values)
### Colours
- Background:       #f4f4f4
- Layer-01:         #ffffff
- Layer-02:         #e8e8e8
- Text-primary:     #161616
- Text-secondary:   #525252
- Text-placeholder: #a8a8a8
- Interactive:      #0f62fe  ← primary blue, use for links and focus
- Interactive hover:#0353e9
- Support-error:    #da1e28
- Support-success:  #198038
- Support-warning:  #f1c21b
- Support-info:     #0043ce
- Border-subtle:    #e0e0e0
- Border-strong:    #8d8d8d

### Spacing (always use multiples of 4px, prefer 8px base)
- sp-01: 2px  | sp-02: 4px  | sp-03: 8px  | sp-04: 16px
- sp-05: 24px | sp-06: 32px | sp-07: 40px | sp-08: 48px

### Typography (IBM Plex Sans only)
- body-01:    14px / 400
- body-02:    16px / 400
- heading-01: 14px / 600
- heading-02: 16px / 600
- productive-heading-03: 20px / 400
- label-01:   12px / 400
- helper-text: 12px / 400, color: text-secondary

## Rules the agent must follow
1. No border-radius on components (Carbon is flat and square). Exceptions: Tags = 2px, Toggle = 14px.
2. Never use arbitrary hex colours. Use only the tokens listed above.
3. Always use IBM Plex Sans. Never introduce another font.
4. Labels always sit ABOVE inputs, never beside them.
5. Use Tag components for status values (Active=green, Error=red, Pending=blue, Archived=gray).
6. Use Stack component for vertical spacing inside forms.
7. Buttons: primary for the single main action only. Never two primary buttons side by side.
8. Modal for critical actions only. Use InlineNotification for feedback within the page.
9. When generating a new story file, follow this structure exactly:

```jsx
export default {
  title: 'Carbon / ComponentName',
  tags: ['autodocs'],
  parameters: {
    docs: {
      description: {
        component: 'One sentence explaining what this component is for and when to use it.',
      },
    },
  },
};

export const StoryName = {
  name: 'Human readable name',
  parameters: {
    docs: {
      description: {
        story: 'One sentence explaining what this specific story demonstrates.',
      },
    },
  },
  render: () => ( /* component here */ ),
};
```

## Grid rules (CRITICAL for layout generation)
- Always use Grid + Column from @carbon/react — never CSS flexbox/grid directly for page layouts
- 16 columns total at lg breakpoint
- Common spans: 16 (full), 8+8 (halves), 4+4+4+4 (quarters), 4+12 (sidebar+content)
- Always set sm, md, lg props together for responsive layouts: <Column sm={4} md={4} lg={8}>
- Gutter modes: default=wide (32px), narrow (16px), condensed (1px)
- Column spans at each breakpoint must add up to 16 (lg), 8 (md), 4 (sm)

## Tabs rules
- Always use composable API: Tabs > TabList > Tab and Tabs > TabPanels > TabPanel
- Line tabs (default): <TabList aria-label="..."> with no extra props
- Contained tabs: <TabList contained aria-label="...">
- Never use the old type="container" prop (deprecated in v11)

## Dropdown rules
- Short fixed list (< 10 items): use Dropdown
- Long list or user benefits from filtering: use ComboBox
- Multiple selections valid: use MultiSelect
- Always provide titleText (label above) and itemToString prop

## Loading rules  
- Full page processing: use Loading with withOverlay={false} (or true for overlay)
- Inline action feedback: use InlineLoading — show active → finished → error states
- Content placeholder while data loads: use SkeletonText, SkeletonPlaceholder, or DataTableSkeleton
- Never use a plain spinner div — always use Carbon's Loading components

## UI Shell rules
- Always wrap Header + SideNav inside HeaderContainer (manages toggle state)
- SideNav isPersistent={true} for always-visible; isPersistent={false} for toggleable
- Always include SkipToContent inside Header for accessibility
- HeaderSideNavItems mirrors Header nav links inside SideNav for mobile
1. Create a new file in src/stories/ComponentName.stories.jsx
2. Import from @carbon/react only
3. Export a default with title under the 'Carbon /' prefix
4. Write at least: a Playground story (with args), an All States story, and one real usage story
5. Run npm run storybook — it hot-reloads automatically

## Storybook structure
src/stories/
  Button.stories.jsx       — 5 variants, 5 sizes, icon, icon-only, disabled
  TextInput.stories.jsx    — default, all 4 states, sizes, password
  Notification.stories.jsx — inline, toast, actionable (all 4 kinds)
  DataTable.stories.jsx    — basic table, toolbar + live search, status tags
  Modal.stories.jsx        — default, danger, form modal, passive
  Tag.stories.jsx          — all 12 colour types, status pattern, sizes
  Form.stories.jsx         — complete login form, settings form
